From 54591515f983293be91f5412dbd8f3607912efac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@advantech.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:21:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] imx8mp_evk: enable PCA9450 I2C level translator in SPL

On RSB-3720 the S-35390A RTC on I2C1 sits behind the PCA9450 I2C level
translator. U-Boot leaves the translator in its reset state, and Linux
enables it only when the pca9450 driver probes (nxp,i2c-lt-enable), a
few milliseconds before the RTC on the same bus probes. The first RTC
access then fails ("error resetting chip", -EIO) and rtc0 is never
registered.

Enable the translator in RUN and STANDBY (the value Linux writes) in
power_init_board(), so it is stable long before the kernel starts.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific, RSB-3720 on imx8mp_evk board code]
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Tsukerman <miketsukerman@advantech.com>
---
 board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/spl.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/spl.c b/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/spl.c
index 165a8cf585f..ab496234478 100644
--- a/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/spl.c
+++ b/board/freescale/imx8mp_evk/spl.c
@@ -117,6 +117,13 @@ int power_init_board(void)
 	pmic_reg_write(dev, PCA9450_BUCK6OUT, 0x18);
 #endif
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep the I2C level translator enabled in RUN and STANDBY before
+	 * Linux probes devices behind it.
+	 */
+	pmic_clrsetbits(dev, PCA9450_CONFIG2, 0x03, 0x01);
+
+
 	return 0;
 }
 #endif
